We analyze the 2D Navier-Stokes equations on the 2D torus with stochastic forces and establish key relationships between the maximum norms of the solution and the initial conditions, including the L^p norm's independence from time. Additionally, our results cover the stochastic Navier-Stokes equations under the following conditions: 
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Low-regularity noise:} 2D torus with p > 1, 
    \item \textbf{High-regularity noise:} any compact domain with p = 1.
\end{itemize}
We also obtain norm-independence results for the stochastic Navier-Stokes equations on various domains, including bounded convex sets and irrational tori.
